ed. I did not edit the four test files, and existing tests pass unchanged.\n\nChanges are in `src/tox/config/set_env.py`, `loader/api.py`, `loader/ini/replace.py`, `loader/toml/_api.py`, `loader/toml/_replace.py` and `sets.py`. Nothing is committed.\n\nWhere the spec left room, I made these calls:\n\n- **INI reference with an emptied base:** if factor filtering empties a referenced `set_env`, the value becomes `\"\"` and any appended override still applies. This is what the `win: MAGIC=base` case needs.\n- **TOML reference with overrides:** the referenced value goes straight to `set_env_reference`, which unrolls it during build. Routing it through the normal recursion made the `_refs` cycle guard fire first, so the spec's \"circular set_env reference\" message never appeared.\n- **Env-file parse errors:** `_extract_key_value` now raises `Fail`, as the spec says. `_extract_key_value_marker` still raises `ValueError`, since the string-line path catches it.\n- **Export iteration:** `__iter__` snapshots the unmaterialized exports before yielding, so a callback that loads another export doesn't drop keys.\n\nI did not run ruff: `ruff` wasn't available through `.venv/bin/python`, so lint and format are unchecked. I also only ran `tests/config`, as the spec lists; the rest of the suite is unverified.", "ttft_ms": 1651, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 298363, "uuid": "69d3d7a6-7283-4fb1-be45-9961ec5f0004", "ttft_stream_ms": 1516, "time_to_request_ms": 325, "first_content_frame_ms": 1516, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
